 "brief": "# build-own-login: every headless build keeps its own Claude login\n\nBrett, Nov 5 2026 (voice): \"Yeah, it should be like that already.\" (after two builds died with 'Not logged in' because he logged the VPS Claude out to add another account).\n\n## Problem\nEvery headless build (deploy/claude-headless.sh via axHub vps.build_start, the orchestrator / agent-swarm launchers, console Terminal headless tabs) runs `claude -p` against the one shared login under the root user's ~/.claude. Logging out, switching accounts or adding an account on the VPS kills or re-points every running build.\n\n## Fix\n- At launch, snapshot the active saved account's credentials (from the claude-accounts store, /root/.claude-accounts, or the live login) into a private per-build config dir (0700, inside or beside the build folder, git-ignored, never committed) and run `claude` with CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR pointed at it. Find the right mechanism for the installed Claude Code version; verify it.\n- Unset any inherited CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN in the launched process so the snapshot wins.\n- Record which account (name + email, never a credential) each build runs on: build log header, orchestrator build note, the build card / Live sessions.\n- Token refresh writes back only to the build's own copy. Delete the copy when the build session ends.\n- Option to pick the account per launch (default: active).\n- Cover every launcher: deploy/claude-headless.sh, orchestrator launch, agent swarm, console headless tabs. Grep for `claude -p`.\n- Test: start a fake build, log the shared login out / switch account, the build keeps its login (scripted test with a fake claude binary). Never print a token.\n\nCoordinate with build claude-accounts-fix-r3 (same day, claude-accounts plugin); don't edit the plugin's save/use logic here.\n\nDone: PR to main, report `_claude/builds/reports/build-own-login.md`, THREADS row, readme, hand to the merge queue (don't merge). No sub-agents, Opus only, never print secrets. Short plain report at the end.",
