 "report": "_claude/builds/reports/build-own-login.md",
 "open": [
  "Refresh-token rotation: if Anthropic rotates refresh tokens, a long build that refreshes its copy and the shared login that refreshes its own can't both stay valid forever on the same account; each is fine on its own, which is the point of this build. Accounts saved with a long-lived token (`claude setup-token`, the switcher's `token`) avoid it.",
  "An unsaved new login on the VPS (logged in as someone else, not saved yet) is taken as the active account's live copy; the claude-accounts plugin already warns about that state and refuses switching until it is saved.",
  "A crashed inner run (kill -9) leaves its copy in `.axf-claude/`; it goes with the worktree, and the next run with the same session name replaces it."
 ]
